# Production WV_TEST_* fault-injection hooks — the complete inventory.
#
# These are deliberately LOCAL: each lives at the site it perturbs, takes exact
# values, and is greppable by name. There is no shared runtime fault dispatcher,
# because these hooks cross different ownership boundaries and a central
# dispatcher would hide that.
#
# Every hook requires the master opt-in WV_TEST_MODE=1 as well as its own exact
# value. Set without WV_TEST_MODE=1 a hook is ignored (with a warning) so a
# stray value in a real environment cannot divert real behaviour; set with it,
# an unrecognised value is an error rather than a silent bypass or no-op.
#
# tests/test-test-hook-registry.sh fails if production code gains a WV_TEST_*
# hook that is not listed here, or if a listed hook no longer appears in the
# file that claims to own it. Adding a hook means adding a line here.
#
# That audit is INVENTORY ONLY. It cannot show that a hook is gated or that it
# validates its value -- grep finding "WV_TEST_MODE" in a file does not
# distinguish a guard from a comment. Each hook's gating and rejection are
# asserted behaviourally in the suite that owns it.
#
# Validation must run BEFORE any conditional branch in its command. Both the
# impact and orphan-classifier hooks originally validated inside the branch
# that executes the fault, so an unrecognised value was accepted on a cache hit
# and on a sweep with no orphans respectively -- the ordinary fast paths.
#
# format: NAME | owning file | allowed values | purpose
WV_TEST_MODE | (master) | 1 | Master opt-in. Every hook below is inert without it.
WV_TEST_SYNC_STUB | scripts/cmd/wv-cmd-data.sh | ok,fail:state,fail:nodes,fail:edges | Stands in for a succeeding GitHub step so the post-sync projection and stamping path is reachable offline, and forces one projection to fail.
WV_TEST_FAIL_ORPHAN_KINDS | scripts/cmd/wv-cmd-data.sh | 1 | Forces the orphan-kind classifier to fail as a whole, a branch unreachable from the CLI.
WV_TEST_IMPACT_RACE | scripts/cmd/wv-cmd-graph.sh | 1 | Mutates the graph during the impact walk, the window the cache publication check exists to close.
